Is it possible to define an additional ssz container so the encoding is less ambiguous? for example:

```rust
#[derive(SszEncode, SszDecode)]
struct MockProof {
    pub public_values: ProgressiveList<u8>,
    pub proof: ProgressiveList<u8>,
}
```

and I'd imagine the CL will do:

```rust
fn verify_execution_proof(
    &self,
    proof_type: u8,
    proof_data: &[u8],
) -> Result<Vec<u8>> {
    let public_values = if self.mock_proof {
        if let Ok(mock_proof) = MockProof::from_ssz_bytes(proof_data) {
            // use public_values from mock proof
            mock_proof.public_values.into_inner()
        } else {
            // fallback to real proof
            self.ere_verifiers[&proof_type].verify(proof_data)?.to_vec()
        }
    } else {
        // default to real proof
        self.ere_verifiers[&proof_type].verify(proof_data)?.to_vec()
    };
    Ok(public_values)
}
```
